# SEO, Accessibility & Performance

Apply when creating or changing public pages, routes, metadata, or UI. Skip pure library/CLI-only changes that have no user-facing web surface — but apply fully to docs sites, landing pages, and apps.

## Technical SEO

- Every indexable page: unique `<title>`, useful meta description, HTTPS canonical, correct robots/noindex.
- Do not leave placeholder titles (`Create Next App`, etc.) or accidental `noindex` on public pages.
- Clean readable URL slugs; preserve indexed URLs with redirects when restructuring.
- Meaningful internal links with descriptive anchors; fix broken links when found.
- Maintain `/sitemap.xml` (canonical HTTPS public URLs only) and `/robots.txt` (do not block critical public assets; sitemap referenced).
- Open Graph (+ Twitter where useful): `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:type`, `og:url`, working `og:image`.
- One primary `<h1>` per page; logical `h2`/`h3` hierarchy — not for styling alone.
- Add accurate Schema.org JSON-LD only when it matches real visible content.
- Production metadata must use HTTPS production domains — never localhost/dev URLs.

## Images & performance

- Meaningful `alt` text (empty `alt=""` only for decorative).
- Modern formats, sized/responsive images; lazy-load below-fold; avoid unnecessary heavy deps.
- Optimize for LCP, INP, CLS; watch TTFB, JS/CSS weight, fonts, third-party scripts.

## Accessibility & mobile

- Semantic HTML, keyboard nav, visible focus, labeled forms, sufficient contrast, usable touch targets.
- Prefer real semantics over ARIA; respect `prefers-reduced-motion` where appropriate.
- Layouts must work on mobile, tablet, and desktop (no overflow, broken nav, untappable controls).
